From 592b80f8d18d0fd3b125039edc03d3aabe394897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <james@generalinference.xyz>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:31:01 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] model : add DSpine block-parallel drafter support

Port Tencent's DSpine (arXiv 2609.36173, 'Draft in Parallel, Condition
Through Depth') to the DFlash draft architecture:

- per-layer code bridge: gated predecessor features injected into the
  next row through network depth, fusing the next layer's input RMSNorm
- serial last-write refinement: fp32 K x K transition table over the
  top-K candidates, packed into the nextn lattice in the DFlash2 walk
  layout
- GGUF conversion for DSpineDraftModel checkpoints (code_bridge
  metadata, dspine_* tensors, version-tensor validation)
- --spec-type draft-dspine alias sharing the DFlash speculative walk

Validated with tencent/Qwen3-8B-DSpine-b16 against Qwen3-8B BF16:
greedy output is token-for-token identical to non-speculative decoding,
~28%% draft acceptance on technical prompts, up to 2.0x generation
speedup (58 vs 28.5 tok/s, Metal, Apple Silicon).

Assisted-by: goose
