diff --git a/docs/speculative.md b/docs/speculative.md
index ffb1e34c7..9d4d10026 100644
--- a/docs/speculative.md
+++ b/docs/speculative.md
@@ -114,6 +114,39 @@ See:
 
 - #25173
 
+### DSpine (`draft-dspine`)
+
+DSpine is a DFlash-family block-parallel drafter: the draft still decodes a whole block of tokens
+in a single forward pass, but a per-layer _code bridge_ conditions each row of the block on its
+predecessor through the network depth (adjacent causal injection). Each row's hidden state reads a
+gated message from the previous row built from a learned codebook, so the block decode recovers
+left-to-right signal without extra passes. After the block logits are produced, a serial
+_last-write refinement_ rebuilds the final layer's write in fp32 for every (sender, receiver)
+candidate pair, yielding a K x K transition table over the top-K candidates per row. The sampler
+walks this lattice greedily, so the accepted prefix is chosen from the full candidate lattice
+rather than from the single top-1 path.
+
+The draft is a small Tencent checkpoint trained for a specific target (for example
+[`tencent/Qwen3-8B-DSpine-b16`](https://huggingface.co/tencent/Qwen3-8B-DSpine-b16) for
+`Qwen/Qwen3-8B`). Convert it with `--target-model-dir` so it inherits the target's tokenizer and
+token embeddings:
+
+```bash
+python convert_hf_to_gguf.py tencent/Qwen3-8B-DSpine-b16 \
+    --target-model-dir Qwen/Qwen3-8B --outtype bf16 --outfile Qwen3-8B-DSpine.gguf
+
+llama-server -m Qwen3-8B.gguf -md Qwen3-8B-DSpine.gguf \
+    --spec-type draft-dspine --spec-draft-n-max 15 -fa on --jinja
+```
+
+`--spec-draft-n-max` is clamped to the draft model's trained block size. DSpine checkpoints are
+also accepted as `--spec-type draft-dflash`: the code bridge and refinement lattice are detected
+from the draft model's tensors, and `draft-dspine` is an alias for the same implementation.
+
+See:
+
+- arXiv 2609.36173 (Draft in Parallel, Condition Through Depth: Adjacent Causal Injection)
+
 ### n-gram Cache (`ngram-cache`)
 
 An n-gram is a sequence of n tokens. The n-gram cache implementation maintains statistics about short n-gram sequences.
